Modern kernel builds force-inject compiler_types.h via -include on the
command line for every compiled object (see c_flags in scripts/Makefile.lib),
which never goes through <linux/compiler.h>. The old guard here assumes
compiler_types.h always sets __LINUX_COMPILER_TYPES_H via that path first,
which is no longer true, so it fires a hard #error on every host-tool build
(scripts/mod/*). The guard is vestigial for a kernel this modern; strip it.

--- a/include/linux/compiler-gcc.h
+++ b/include/linux/compiler-gcc.h
@@ -1,7 +1,4 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 */
-#ifndef __LINUX_COMPILER_TYPES_H
-#error "Please don't include <linux/compiler-gcc.h> directly, include <linux/compiler.h> instead."
-#endif
 
 /*
  * Common definitions for all gcc versions go here.
